om/zopefoundation/zope.sqlalchemy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/zopefoundation/zope.sqlalchemy","homepage":"","size":249,"stargazers_count":34,"watchers_count":34,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":39,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":8,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["integration","maintained","pyramid","python","sqlalchemy","transaction","zope"],"visibility":"public","forks":39,"open_issues":8,"watchers":34,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"## BUG/PROBLEM REPORT (OR OTHER COMMON ISSUE)\r\n\r\nUnder SQLAlchemy 1.4, `keep_session=True` is broken.  \r\n\r\nA SQLAlchemy Session is registered to `transaction` via `zope.sqlalchemy`, with `keep_session` set to `True`.\r\n\r\nEditing an object in the session and calling `.flush` will cause SQLAlchemy to invoke a commit on the actual session - not the unit of work - and trigger the before_commit hook in zope.sqlalchemy, which will then fail.\r\n\r\nRelavent LOC from stack trace:\r\n\r\n* https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/master/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/session.py#L3360\r\n* https://github.com/zopefoundation/zope.sqlalchemy/blob/master/src/zope/sqlalchemy/datamanager.py#L300-L304\r\n\r\n\r\n### What I did:\r\n\r\nreproducible test case below\r\n\r\n### What I expect to happen:\r\n\r\nThe session should flush as in SQLAlchemy 1.3, not commit.\r\n\r\n### What actually happened:\r\n\r\nSQLAlchemy invoked a commit on the transaction.\r\n\r\n### What version of Python and Zope/Addons I am using:\r\n\r\n* Python3.8\r\n* zope.sqlalchemy==1.3\r\n* sqlalchemy==1.4\r\n\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom zope.sqlalchemy import register\r\nimport transaction\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import (\r\n\tcreate_engine,\r\n\tColumn,\r\n\tInteger,\r\n\tString,\r\n)\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import relationship, sessionmaker\r\n\r\n\r\nengine = create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass User(Base):\r\n\t__tablename__ = \"user\"\r\n\tid = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n\tuser_name = Column(String(50))\r\n\r\n\tdef __repr__(self):\r\n\t\treturn f\"<User(id={self.id}, user_name='{self.user_name}')>\"\r\n\r\n\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(engine)\r\n\r\nSession = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\r\n\r\n# this breaks in 1.4\r\n# session/transaction setup\r\nsession = Session()\r\nregister(session, keep_session=True)\r\n\r\n# add a user\r\nuser = User(user_name=\"User\")\r\nsession.add(user)\r\nsession.flush(objects=[user])\r\ntransaction.commit()\r\ntransaction.begin()\r\n\r\n# edit them\r\nuser.user_name = \"User2\"\r\n\r\n# this raises an AssertionError under SQLAlchemy 1.4\r\nsession.flush(objects=[user])\r\n```\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zopefoundation/zope.sqlalchemy/issues/57/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zopefoundation/zope.sqlalchemy/issues/57/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]